# Lightning Web Component `setState` Method

Use the `setState` method to set the state of the rendered Lightning web component for CRM Analytics dashboards.

## Arguments

| Argument Name | Description                                                     |
| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `state`       | The state to update the CRM Analytics dashboard component with. |

## Example

Add your implementation of the `setState` call into the wrapper Javascript and HTML for your component.

:::note
To use the communityDashboard component, replace `wave-wave-dashboard-lwc` with `wave-community-dashboard`.
:::

The HTML for the component:

```html
<template>
  <lightning-button variant="brand" label="Set Dashboard State" title="Set State Action" onclick={setState} class="slds-m-left_x-small"></lightning-button>
  <wave-wave-dashboard-lwc dashboard="0FK5B000000XiK14AK" height="1000"></wave-wave-dashboard-lwc>
</template>
```

The Javascript for the component, which implements `setState()`:

```javascript
import { LightningElement } from 'lwc';

export default class DashboardWrapper extends LightningElement {
  _state = {};

  setState () {
    const dashboard = this.template.querySelector('wave-wave-dashboard-lwc');
    dashboard.setState(this._state);
    console.warn("setState complete");
  }
}
```

The `state` can be set dynamically from user input or from another dashboard’s `state`. For the complete dashboard `state` structure, refer to the [Analytics Dashboard JSON Reference](https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/atlas.en-us.bi_dev_guide_json.meta/bi_dev_guide_json/bi_dbjson_intro.htm) guide.

